            <h4 data-number="5.2.7.5" id="subject-place"><span
            class="header-section-number">5.2.7.5</span> Subject
            Place</h4>
            <p><strong>Element name:</strong> &lt;<a
            href="http://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectPlace">lido:subjectPlace</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Note:</strong> Subject Place contains information
            about a particular place the object depicts or is about.
            Fictitious places are indexed as &lt;<a
            href="https://lido-schema.org/schema/latest/lido.html#subjectObject">lido:subjectObject</a>&gt;</p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong> The place depicted in
            Leonardo’s Mona Lisa is possibly Bobbio in the Province of
            Piacenza. Coordinates are taken from Wikidata. The subject
            type is “<a
            href="http://terminology.lido-schema.org/lido00136">Identification</a>”.</p>
            <blockquote>
            <p><strong>Subject Place:</strong> Possibly Bobbio in the
            Province of Piacenza<br /> <strong><em>Subject
            Type:</em></strong> Identification<br /> <strong>Place
            Name:</strong> Bobbio <strong><em>Preference:</em></strong>
            Preferred <strong>Coordinates:</strong> 44.7715, 9.3864</p>
            </blockquote>
            <div class="sourceCode" id="cb40"><pre
            class="sourceCode xml"><code class="sourceCode xml"><span id="cb40-1"><a href="#cb40-1" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1"></a>&lt;<span class="kw">lido:subjectSet</span>&gt;</span>
